{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3069","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3069","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3069\",\"parent_revision\":\"a367b8a7c2123340a985f73e1fa2a7900401a4e4f2e667b362de147c236386a9\",\"root_revision\":\"a367b8a7c2123340a985f73e1fa2a7900401a4e4f2e667b362de147c236386a9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Audit all `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` `defaultPrompt` fields across `plugins/*/` for mid-sentence truncation.\\n- [ ] Rewrite each truncated one as complete, accurate prose describing the plugin's default prompt behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a maintainer, I want the `defaultPrompt` fields in `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` files that are currently truncated mid-word/mid-sentence (e.g. development-harness's, cut off at \\\"...with ARL human\\\") rewritten as complete prose, so Codex users see a coherent default prompt instead of leftover truncation artifacts.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced while fixing PR #2787 deferred findings #1/#8/#10/#11 (issue #3049) \u2014 the fix for finding #11 (preserving hand-curated `interface` fields) correctly preserves these values as-is, since they're not derived/generated content, but they were never actually correct \u2014 they're leftovers from an earlier one-off truncation bug, not intentionally curated prose. This is a content quality pass, not a code fix.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"118ca4614d9e1d5e41e376015aaf945721c12b986074e385b0edaec29e0fa158\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcPcw\"}"}